    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15392" root="رزغ" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْزِغٌ</span></b>  Rain <i>that moistens the earth,</i> or <i>ground,
exceeding the ordinary degree, but not flowing;</i>
opposed to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسِيلٌ</span>, “ that causes the valleys and
water-courses (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِلَاع</span>) to flow. ” (S, and Ham *
p. 632.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَزِغٌ</span>.

